<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p>
  Skybook is extensively focused on user privacy and attempts to store as little
  data as possible. All sensitive data we store is either hashed alongside a
  salt, or stored encrypted. As our source code is freely available, data usage
  can be independently verified.
</p>

<h3>Information we collect</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Any information you willingly provide to the service</li>
  <li>A salted hash of your IP address</li>
  <li>All settings and entries on your guestbook</li>
</ul>
<h3>How we use it</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    We use your hashed IP address to provide owners of guestbooks the ability to
    moderate messages
  </li>
</ul>
<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>

Skybook may rely on third-party services to operate the platform, such as
hosting infrastructure.

<h3>Data Retention</h3>
Skybook retains information only for as long as necessary for operation of the
service.

<h3>---</h3>
We retain the right to update this Privacy Policy at any time.

